&Q000386 = The death of Ur-Namma (Ur-Namma A)
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.2.4.1.1
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.2.4.1.1&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

@div version 1 (A version from Nibru)

1.1. [...]-ta kalam teš₂-a mi-ni-ib#-X
#lem: X; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; teš[unity]; X
#tr.en: …… entire land ……, …… struck, the palace was devastated. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.1

1.2. [...]-in#-sag₃ e₂-gal im-sig₁₀-sig₁₀
#lem: sag[strike]; egal[palace]; sig[put into]
#tr.en: …… panic spread rapidly among the dwellings of the black-headed people. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.2

1.3. [...] saŋ# gig₂ tuš-a-ba ni₂ ul₄-la bi₂-ib₂#-te
#lem: X; saŋ[head]; giggig[black]; tuš[sit (down)]; ni[fear]; ul[hasten]; teŋ[approach]
#tr.en: …… abandoned places …… in @wGN{Sumer}. …… the cities were destroyed in their entirety; 
#etcsl: line-id=1.3

1.4. X X X X X ki-šub-ba-bi ki-en-gi-ra bi₂-ib-ŋar
#lem: X; X; X; X; X; kišuba[waste ground]; Kengir[1]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: the people were seized with panic. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.4

1.5. X niŋ₂#-daŋal-ba iri ba#-an-gul uŋ₃-e ni₂ bi₂-in-te
#lem: X; niŋdaŋala[vastness]; iri[city]; gul[destroy]; uŋ[people]; ni[fear]; teŋ[approach]
#tr.en: Evil came upon @wSN{Urim} and made the trustworthy shepherd pass away. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.5

1.6. urim₅#{ki}-ma hul-ŋal₂ im-ši-DU sipad zid ba-ra-ab-e₃
#lem: Urim[1]SN; huluŋal[evil]; X; sipad[shepherd]; zid[right]; e[leave]
#tr.en: It made @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Namma}}, the trustworthy shepherd, pass away; 
#etcsl: line-id=1.6

1.7. sipad# zid# ur-{d}namma# ba#-ra-ab-e₃ sipad zid ba-ra-ab-e₃
#lem: sipad[shepherd]; zid[right]; Urnamma[1]RN; e[leave]; sipad[shepherd]; zid[right]; e[leave]
#tr.en: it made the trustworthy shepherd pass away. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.7

1.8. an#-ne₂ inim kug-ga du₃-a mu-un-kur₂ šag₄ AN X sug₄-ga-am₃
#lem: An[1]DN; inim[word]; kug[pure]; du[build]; kur[different]; šag[heart]; X; X; sug[empty]
#tr.en: Because @wDN{An} had altered his holy words completely, …… became empty, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.8

1.9. {d}en#-lil₂-le nam tar-ra du₃-a šu# lul [mi]-ni-ib-bal
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; nam[fate]; tar[cut]; du[build]; šu[hand]; lul[false]; bala[turn]
#tr.en: and because, deceitfully, @wDN{Enlil} had completely changed the fate he decreed, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.9

1.10. {d}nin-mah#-e X [...] X LA₂-A-BA-na a-nir mu-un-ŋa₂-ŋa₂
#lem: Ninmah[1]DN; X; X; X; X; anir[lament]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: @wDN{Ninmaḫ} began a lament in her ……. @wDN{Enki} shut (?) the great door of @wSN{Eridug}. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.10

1.11. {d}en-ki-ke₄# {ŋiš}ig# gal eridug{ki}-ga gu₂-bi ba-an-gi₄
#lem: Enkik[1]DN; ig[door]; gal[big]; Eridug[1]SN; gu[neck]; gi[turn]
#tr.en: @wDN{Nudimmud} withdrew into his bedchamber and lay down fasting. At his zenith, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.11

1.12. {d}nu-dim₂-mud# itima#{ma}-a-ka ba-an-kur₉ šag₄-ka-tab-ba ba-an-nu₂
#lem: Nudimmud[1]DN; itima[sleeping chamber]; kur[enter]; šakatab[fasting]; nud[lie down]
#tr.en: @wDN{Nanna} frowned at the …… words of @wDN{An}. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.12

1.13. inim X an-na-ka# {d}nanna si-un₃-na saŋ-ki ba-da-ni-in-gid₂
#lem: inim[word]; X; An[1]DN; Nanna[1]DN; siʾuna[zenith]; saŋki[forehead]; gid[long]
#tr.en: @wDN{Utu} did not come forth in the sky, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.13

1.14. {d}utu an-na# nu-um-ed₂-e ud-de₃ i-si-iš im-la₂
#lem: Utu[1]DN; an[sky]; e[leave]; ud[sun]; isiš[tears]; la[hang]
#tr.en: and the day was full of sorrow. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.14

1.15. ama dumu-ni-še₃ hul til₃-la-e
#lem: ama[mother]; dumu[child]; hulu[bad]; til[live (of a single person)]
#tr.en: The mother, miserable because of her son, the mother of the king, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.15

1.16. ama# lugal#-la kug# {d}nin-sumun₂-na a šag₄-ŋu₁₀ im-me
#lem: ama[mother]; lugal[king]; kug[purify]; Ninsumunak[1]DN; aya[cry]; šag[heart]; dug[speak]
#tr.en: holy @wDN{Ninsumun}, was crying: @q[Ninsumun,]{“Oh my heart!”}. Because of the fate decreed for @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Namma}}, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.16

1.17. nam# ur-{d}namma mu-un-tar-ra-še₃
#lem: nam[fate]; Urnamma[1]RN; tar[cut]
#tr.en: because it made the trustworthy shepherd pass away, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.17

1.18. mu# sipad zid ba-ra-ab-e₃-a-še₃
#lem: mu[name]; sipad[shepherd]; zid[right]; e[leave]
#tr.en: she was weeping bitterly in the broad square, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.18

1.19. sila# daŋal ki-a-ne-di ŋal₂-la-ba er₂# gig# i₃-še₈-še₈
#lem: sila[street]; daŋal[wide]; kiʾenedi[play area]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]; er[tears]; gig[sick]; šeš[weep]
#tr.en: which is otherwise a place of entertainment. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.19

1.20. nam-lu₂-ulu₃ X li-bi [...] X X u₃ dug₃ nu-mu-un-ku-ku
#lem: namlulu[humanity]; X; lib[happy]; X; X; X; u[sleep]; dug[good]; ku[place]
#tr.en: Sweet sleep did not come to the people whose happiness ……; 
#etcsl: line-id=1.20

1.21. i-lu# sipad# zid ba-dab₅-ba-na ud mi-ni-ib-zal-e
#lem: ilu[lament]; sipad[shepherd]; zid[right]; dab[seize]; ud[sun]; zal[pass time]
#tr.en: they passed their time in lamentation over the trustworthy shepherd who had been snatched away. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.21

1.22. a-eštub# id₂#-da de₂-a-bi ku₃-ŋal₂-bi ba-sig₉
#lem: aʾeštub[early flooding]; id[river]; de[pour]; guŋal[inspector]; sig[silent]
#tr.en: As the early flood was filling the canals, their canal-inspector was already silenced (?); 
#etcsl: line-id=1.22

1.23. [še gu]-nu a-gar₃-re mu₂-a-bi# zi kalam-ma ba-su
#lem: še[barley]; gunu[qualification of barley]; agar[meadow]; mu[grow]; zi[life]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; su[sink]
#tr.en: the mottled barley grown on the arable lands, the life of the land, was inundated. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.23

1.24. [engar] gana₂# zid-de₃# gub-X-ni mu-na-ab-tur-re
#lem: engar[farmer]; gana[field]; zid[right]; gub[stand]; tur[small]
#tr.en: To the farmer, the fertile fields planted (?) by him yielded little. @wDN{Enkimdu}, the lord of levees and ditches, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.24

1.25. {[d]}[en-ki-im-du lugal eg₂ pa₅-ra-ke₄] urim₂#{ki}-ta# eg₂# pa₅ ba-da-an-kar
#lem: Enkimdu[1]DN; lugal[king]; eg[levee]; par[(small) canal]; Urim[1]SN; eg[levee]; par[(small) canal]; kar[flee]
#tr.en: took away the levees and ditches from @wSN{Urim}. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.25

1.26. NA [...] X X X PI X [...] X ki bi₂-in-tag
#lem: X; X; X; X; X; X; X; X; X; ki[place]; tag[touch]
#tr.en: As the intelligence and …… of the Land were lost, fine food became scarce. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.26

1.27. umuš X kalam-ma [u₂]-gu# im-ma-an-de₂# u₂ nir-ŋal₂ ba-sug₄
#lem: umuš[consideration]; X; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; ugu[cvne]; de[pour]; u[plant(s)]; nirŋal[authoritative]; sug[empty]
#tr.en: The plains did not grow lush grass any more, they grew the grass of mourning. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.27

1.28. edin-edin-e u₂ sag₉#-[ga] nu-mu-un-mu₂# u₂-a-nir ba-an-mu₂
#lem: eden[back]; u[plant(s)]; sag[good]; mu[grow]; anir[grass]; mu[grow]
#tr.en: The cows ……, their …… cattle-pen has been destroyed. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.28

1.29. ab₂-e# X [...] mu-un-X tur₃ X-bi ba-gul
#lem: ab[cow]; X; X; X; tur[animal stall]; X; gul[destroy]
#tr.en: The calves …… their cows bleated bitterly. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.29

1.30. amar ab₂-šilam#-[...] mur# gig-ga#-bi im-ša₄
#lem: amar[calf]; abšilam[cow]; mur[noise]; gig[sick]; ša[cvve]
#etcsl: line-id=1.30

1.31. sipad kug-zu [...] X A [...] X a₂ nu#-[mu]-da-an-aŋ₂-e
#lem: sipad[shepherd]; kugzu[wise]; X; X; X; X; X; a[arm]; aŋ[measure]
#tr.en: The wise shepherd …… does not give orders any more. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.31

1.32. me₃ šen#-[šen-na ...] A SI A# ba#-da-ab#-tab#-e#
#lem: me[battle]; šen[battle]; X; X; X; X; tab[double]
#tr.en: …… in battle and combat. The king, the advocate of @wGN{Sumer}, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.32

1.33. lugal ka-mud-ŋal₂ ki-en#-gi-ra# [me-te unken-na]
#lem: lugal[king]; kamudŋal[advocate]; Kengir[1]; mete[appropriate thing]; unkin[assembly]
#tr.en: the ornament of the assembly, @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Namma}}, the advocate of @wGN{Sumer}, the ornament of the assembly, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.33

1.34. ur-{d}namma ka-mud-ŋal₂# ki-en-[gi-ra me]-te# unken-na
#lem: Urnamma[1]RN; kamudŋal[advocate]; Kengir[1]; mete[appropriate thing]; unkin[assembly]
#tr.en: the leader of @wGN{Sumer}, …… lies sick. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.34

1.35. mas-su ki-en-gi-ra#-ke₄# X [i₃]-nu₂ tur₅-ra-am₃
#lem: massu[leader]; Kengir[1]; X; nud[lie down]; tur[ill]
#tr.en: His hands which used to grasp cannot grasp any more, he lies sick. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.35

1.36. šu-ni dab₅-ba# nu-mu-un#-dab₅# in-nu₂ tur₅-ra-am₃
#lem: šu[hand]; dab[seize]; dab[seize]; nud[lie down]; tur[ill]
#tr.en: His feet …… cannot step any more, he lies sick. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.36

1.37. ŋiri₃#-[ni] X X nu-um-un-da-dib# i₃-nu₂ tur₅-ra-am₃
#lem: ŋiri[foot]; X; X; dib[pass]; nud[lie down]; tur[ill]
#tr.en: The trustworthy shepherd, king, the sword of @wGN{Sumer}, @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Namma}}, the king of the Land, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.37

1.38. [...] X X IM X UŠ [...] saŋ# ME ba-BU
#lem: X; X; X; X; X; X; X; saŋ[head]; X; X
#tr.en: was taken to the …… house. He was taken to @wSN{Urim}; 
#etcsl: line-id=1.38

1.39. sipad zid lugal# ŋiri₂ gal ki-en-gi-ra-ke₄
#lem: sipad[shepherd]; zid[right]; lugal[king]; ŋiri[dagger]; gal[big]; Kengir[1]
#tr.en: the king of the Land was brought into the …… house. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.39

1.40. [ur]-{[d]}[namma] lugal kalam-ma-ke₄ e₂-sumur-ra ba-an-te
#lem: Urnamma[1]RN; lugal[king]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; esumur[lying-in-state room?]; teŋ[approach]
#tr.en: The proud one lay in his palace. @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Namma}}, he who was beloved by the troops, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.40

1.41. urim₂#{[ki]}-ma# im-te ur-{d}namma e₂-zu₂-ra-ah-a# X-kur₉
#lem: Urim[1]SN; teŋ[approach]; Urnamma[1]RN; ezurah[lying-in-state room?]; kur[enter]
#tr.en: could not raise his neck any more. The wise one …… lay down; 
#etcsl: line-id=1.41

1.42. saŋ-kug-ŋal₂# e₂-gal-a-na i₃-nu₂
#lem: saŋguŋal[proud]; egal[palace]; nud[lie down]
#tr.en: silence descended. As he, who was the vigour of the Land, had fallen, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.42

1.43. ur-{d}namma lu₂ erin₂-e ki aŋ₂-ŋa₂ gu₂ nu-mu-un-da-zig₃-ge
#lem: Urnamma[1]RN; lu[person]; erin[people]; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]; gu[neck]; zig[rise]
#tr.en: the Land became demolished like a mountain; like a cypress forest it was stripped, its appearance changed. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.43

1.44. igi-ŋal₂ [X X]-ra i₃-nu₂ ŋiš-la₂-bi im-DU
#lem: igiŋal[wise]; X; X; nud[lie down]; ŋešlabi[silence]; X
#tr.en: As if he were a boxwood tree, they put axes against him in his joyous dwelling place. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.44

1.45. teš₂ kalam-ma-ka ba-šub{ub} hur-saŋ-gin₇ ba-gul
#lem: teš[unity]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; šub[fall]; hursaŋ[mountain]; gul[destroy]
#tr.en: As if he were a sappy cedar tree, he was uprooted in the palace where he used to sleep (?). 
#etcsl: line-id=1.45

1.46. tir# [ha-šu]-ur₂#-ra-gin₇ im-ma-sug₄ me-dim₂-bi ba-kur₂
#lem: tir[forest]; hašur[tree]; sug[empty]; medim[limbs]; kur[different]
#tr.en: His spouse …… resting place; 
#etcsl: line-id=1.46

1.47. {ŋiš}taškarin!(ŠE₃)-gin₇ ki-[tuš giri₁₇-zal]-la#-na giŋ₄ mu-ni-in-ŋar-re-eš
#lem: taškarin[box tree]; kituš[dwelling place]; kirizal[joy]; giŋ[ax]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: …… was covered by a storm; 
#etcsl: line-id=1.47

1.48. {ŋiš}erin duru₅-gin₇ e₂-gal#-[la] nu₂#-a mu-ni-in-bal-bal-e-ne
#lem: eren[cedar]; duru[wet]; egal[palace]; nud[lie down]; bala[turn]
#tr.en: it embraced it like a wife her sweetheart (?). 
#etcsl: line-id=1.48

1.49. ki-nu₂ nitalam-a-ni# ba#-[...] X X X u₁₈-lu-da ba-da-dul
#lem: kinud[sleeping quarter]; ŋidlam[(equal ranking) spouse]; X; X; X; X; ulu[south wind]; dul[cover]
#tr.en: His appointed time had arrived, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.49

1.50. šeš-a#-ni-da dam-a-ni-gin₇# gu₂-da# am₃-mi-ib-la₂
#lem: šeš[brother]; dam[spouse]; gu[neck]; la[hang]
#tr.en: and he passed away in his prime. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.50

1.51. ud dug₄#-ga-ni sa₂ mu-ni-ib#-dug₄ a-la-na ba-ra-e₃#
#lem: ud[sun]; dug[speak]; sa[equal]; dug[speak]; ala[exuberance]; e[leave]
#etcsl: line-id=1.51

1.52. sizkur₂# niŋ₂ dug₃-ga la-ba-an-tag-ge šu gig ba-ni-X-[gid₂]
#lem: siškur[prayer]; niŋ[thing]; dug[good]; tag[touch]; šu[hand]; gig[sick]; gid[long]
#tr.en: His (?) pleasing sacrifices were no longer accepted; they were treated as dirty (?). 
#etcsl: line-id=1.52

1.53. kadra-ni {d}a-nun-na-ke₄-ne inim im-ma-an-gi₄#-[...]
#lem: kadra[greeting gift]; Anunak[1]DN; inim[word]; gi[turn]
#tr.en: The @wDN{Anuna} gods refused his gifts. @wDN{An} did not stand by an @q[An,]{“It is enough”}, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.53

1.54. an muš₃#-am₃# X la-ba-e-gub# ud-bi la-ba-ni-ib-si
#lem: An[1]DN; mušam[(exclamation of) compassion]; X; gub[stand]; ud[sun]; si[fill]
#tr.en: and he could not complete his (?) days. Because of what @wDN{Enlil} ordered, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.54

1.55. inim {d}en#-lil₂-la₂ dug₄-ga-še₃ ur₅ zi-zi# la-ba-ŋal₂
#lem: inim[word]; Enlil[1]DN; dug[speak]; ur[that]; zig[rise]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#tr.en: there was no more rising up; his beloved men lost their wise one. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.55

1.56. nam#-[lu₂]-ulu₃#-ni ki ba-aŋ₂-ŋa₂-bi igi-ŋal₂-bi ba-kur₂
#lem: namlulu[humanity]; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]; igiŋal[wise]; kur[different]
#tr.en: Strangers turned into (?) ……. How iniquitously @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Namma}} was abandoned, like a broken jar! 
#etcsl: line-id=1.56

1.57. X X-la lu₂ nu-zu-u₃-e-ne i-im-bal-bal-e-ne
#lem: X; X; lu[person]; zu[know]; bala[turn]
#tr.en: His …… with grandeur like (?) thick clouds (?). He does not …… any more, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.57

1.58. a-gin₇# ki-lul#-la ur-{d}namma dug gaz-gin₇ a-ba-ni-in-taka₄-aš
#lem: agin[thus]; kilulak[murder]; Urnamma[1]RN; dug[(clay) pot]; gaz[kill]; taka[set aside]
#tr.en: and he does not reach out for ……. @q{“…… @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Namma}}, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.58

1.59. X X-a-ni |IM.UD| sir₂-da-gin₇ gal-bi im-ši-DU
#lem: X; X; IM.UD[cloud?]; sir[dense]; gal[big]; X
#tr.en: alas, what is it to me?”} @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Namma}}, the son of @wDN{Ninsumun}, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.59

1.60. X [X X] X nu-ŋa₂-ŋa₂-a niŋ₂ šag₄-ge šu nu-gid₂-i im-me
#lem: X; X; X; X; ŋar[put]; niŋ[thing]; šag[heart]; šu[hand]; gid[long]; dug[speak]
#tr.en: was brought to @wGN{Arali}, the pre-eminent place of the Land, in his prime. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.60

1.61. X X X ur#-{d}namma me-li-e-a nam-ŋu₁₀
#lem: X; X; X; Urnamma[1]RN; meliʾeʾa[an exclamation]; anam[what]
#tr.en: The soldiers accompanying the king shed tears: 
#etcsl: line-id=1.61

